> TLDR:
>
> GDAL 3.14 (milestoned for ~November 2026) adds a read-only Icechunk
driver and '/vsiicechunk/' virtual filesystem, giving R users access to
versioned cloud-native Zarr stores through GDAL supported packages. The
post walks through reading a 14TB ECMWF AIFS forecast store via gdal mdim
info and its R equivalents,  unpacks GDAL's VSI path model (auth,
addressing, endpoints, and chained prefixes like '/vsizip//vsicurl/') as an
alternative to Icechunk-Python.  It concludes with a brief look at a GDAL
xarray backend and some cross-language questions, with a nod to the growing
R Zarr landscape (pizzarr, Rarr, zarr, CopernicusMarine).
